# Generated review packets (`pnpm review:prep`) are deliberately NOT ignored.
#
# An earlier version ignored `review/*.md`, which silently defeated the whole
# point of the review protocol: `reviewer.md` rule 6 says a rejected finding is
# closed once it is recorded in `review/<sha>.md`, and `review/README.md` says the
# rejections must be written down or the next round re-raises them. If the record
# is gitignored, a fresh clone or any reviewer that did not generate the packet
# locally cannot see it — so rule 6 can never fire and every rejected finding
# comes back. That is the exact spiral this machinery exists to end.
#
# Packets are small (a diff and a checklist) and carry no secrets; they are the
# audit trail of the review, so they belong in version control.
#
# Only the free-text scratch report from the flake gate is ignored.

# Agent working documents — local only, never committed
RESTRUCTURE-PLAN.md
SPEC-CLASSIFICATION.md
